msgstr "Other (hex code)..."

msgctxt "#30025"
msgid "Button's hex code: enable debug logging, press the button, and look in the log for a line like '... (0xXXXX, obc-NNNNN) pressed...'. Type the 0xXXXX part here (with or without '0x'); the obc-NNNNN number does NOT work, it's for reference only."
msgstr "Button's hex code: enable debug logging, press the button, and look in the log for a line like '... (0xXXXX, obc-NNNNN) pressed...'. Type the 0xXXXX part here (with or without '0x'); the obc-NNNNN number does NOT work, it's for reference only."

msgctxt "#30026"
msgid "Invalid hexadecimal code."
msgstr "Invalid hexadecimal code."

msgctxt "#30027"
msgid "Detect by pressing the button..."
msgstr "Detect by pressing the button..."

msgctxt "#30028"
msgid "On the next screen, press the remote button you want to use as the hotkey ONCE. You have 15 seconds; press Back to cancel. Only works on Kodi 21 'Omega' or newer."
msgstr "On the next screen, press the remote button you want to use as the hotkey ONCE. You have 15 seconds; press Back to cancel. Only works on Kodi 21 'Omega' or newer."

msgctxt "#30029"
msgid "Could not detect a usable code for that button. Your Kodi version may not support this (Kodi 21 'Omega' or newer is required) -- use 'Other (hex code)...' with the log method instead."
msgstr "Could not detect a usable code for that button. Your Kodi version may not support this (Kodi 21 'Omega' or newer is required) -- use 'Other (hex code)...' with the log method instead."

msgctxt "#30030"
msgid "Code detected"
msgstr "Code detected"

msgctxt "#30031"
msgid "Use this button as the hotkey?"
msgstr "Use this button as the hotkey?"

msgctxt "#30032"
msgid "Equalizer APO was not detected on this computer (check Settings > config.txt path if you think this is wrong). It's required: this addon only writes the mix into its configuration, Equalizer APO is what actually applies it to the audio.\n\nIt can be downloaded and installed now (the official installer from equalizerapo.com via SourceForge will open; Windows may ask for administrator permission)."
msgstr "Equalizer APO was not detected on this computer (check Settings > config.txt path if you think this is wrong). It's required: this addon only writes the mix into its configuration, Equalizer APO is what actually applies it to the audio.\n\nIt can be downloaded and installed now (the official installer from equalizerapo.com via SourceForge will open; Windows may ask for administrator permission)."

msgctxt "#30033"
msgid "Install it now"
msgstr "Install it now"

msgctxt "#30034"
msgid "I already have it installed"
msgstr "I already have it installed"

msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Install Equalizer APO..."
msgstr "Install Equalizer APO..."

msgctxt "#30036"
msgid "Could not download Equalizer APO:\n%s\n\nYou can download and install it yourself from https://equalizerapo.com/"
msgstr "Could not download Equalizer APO:\n%s\n\nYou can download and install it yourself from https://equalizerapo.com/"

msgctxt "#30037"
msgid "The Equalizer APO installer has been launched. Follow its steps (it may ask for administrator permission) and pick the output device you want to use it on. When it finishes, Windows may ask you to log off or restart. Afterwards, open this addon again."
msgstr "The Equalizer APO installer has been launched. Follow its steps (it may ask for administrator permission) and pick the output device you want to use it on. When it finishes, Windows may ask you to log off or restart. Afterwards, open this addon again."
